{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"c15bd4dc4e1146fe","name":"card_unit_54_jager_regiment","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/Breakthrough/units/card_unit_54_jager_regiment","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"56. JÄGER REGIMENT","text":"Pincer: -1 Operation Cost.","flavorText":"The 56th Jäger Regiment, formally known as 56th Infantry Regiment, was formed in France 1941. The regiment was placed under the 5th Light Division and then in July 1942 the name was changed to 5th Jäger Division. The division fought on the Eastern Front from where it would retreat back to Germany in 1944. In 1945 the division fought in defensive battles in Germany and surrendered to the Red Army near Oder River during the Battle of Berlin. Jäger divisions (Jäger means hunter in German) of the Wehrmacht were highly trained and used to operate where smaller units were needed, in rough terrain, foothills, urban areas, and were more heavily equipped than mountain divisions. At the start of the war Jäger divisions had three regiments, but by 1942 they were downsized to two.","faction":"Germany","type":"infantry","rarity":"Common","cost":1,"operationCost":1,"attack":2,"defense":1},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_54_jager_regiment","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_54_jager_regiment_title","SourceString":"56. JÄGER REGIMENT","LocalizedString":"56. JÄGER REGIMENT"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":2,"defense":1,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_54_jager_regiment_text","SourceString":"Pincer: -1 Operation Cost.","LocalizedString":"Pincer: -1 Operation Cost."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_54_jager_regiment_history","SourceString":"The 56th Jäger Regiment, formally known as 56th Infantry Regiment, was formed in France 1941. The regiment was placed under the 5th Light Division and then in July 1942 the name was changed to 5th Jäger Division. The division fought on the Eastern Front from where it would retreat back to Germany in 1944. In 1945 the division fought in defensive battles in Germany and surrendered to the Red Army near Oder River during the Battle of Berlin. Jäger divisions (Jäger means hunter in German) of the Wehrmacht were highly trained and used to operate where smaller units were needed, in rough terrain, foothills, urban areas, and were more heavily equipped than mountain divisions. At the start of the war Jäger divisions had three regiments, but by 1942 they were downsized to two.","LocalizedString":"The 56th Jäger Regiment, formally known as 56th Infantry Regiment, was formed in France 1941. The regiment was placed under the 5th Light Division and then in July 1942 the name was changed to 5th Jäger Division. The division fought on the Eastern Front from where it would retreat back to Germany in 1944. In 1945 the division fought in defensive battles in Germany and surrendered to the Red Army near Oder River during the Battle of Berlin. Jäger divisions (Jäger means hunter in German) of the Wehrmacht were highly trained and used to operate where smaller units were needed, in rough terrain, foothills, urban areas, and were more heavily equipped than mountain divisions. At the start of the war Jäger divisions had three regiments, but by 1942 they were downsized to two."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Breakthrough","isReserved":true,"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Pincer"],"hasPincer":true,"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Explosion02'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/StarterContent/Audio/Explosion02.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Germany/CandidateArtwork/WE_Candidates/t_5th_jager.t_5th_jager","SubPathString":""},"artist":"David Pentland","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/56__JÄGER_REGIMENT.56__JÄGER_REGIMENT","SubPat